<title>USA: Vail Resorts shares fall off peak.</title>
<headline>Vail Resorts shares fall off peak.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vail Resorts Inc, which rose 10 percent on its first day of trading in a highly-touted initial public offering, &quot;broke issue&quot; on its third day of trading.</p>
<p>The shares fell 1 to 21 on Friday.  A &quot;broken IPO&quot; is one that falls below the price where investors bought the stock from the underwriters.</p>
</text>
